WEBVTT

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:02.870
I shall grant you this!

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:21.280
That's a magical violin.

00:01:56.610 --> 00:01:59.300
The Impending Troubles of Gavotte

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:03.680
Come on, hurry and play for us.

00:02:12.390 --> 00:02:14.580
Huh? Why?

00:02:15.050 --> 00:02:18.530
Didn't he say this was a magical violin that anyone can play?

00:02:19.170 --> 00:02:20.950
What the heck is that?!

00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:24.500
Do you have no intention of playing for us?

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:26.560
N-No...

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:28.790
OK, that's enough.

00:02:30.430 --> 00:02:32.320
You all right, Hino-chan?

00:02:33.030 --> 00:02:34.500
Oh, I met him in the faculty room...

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:35.640
Yunoki-sama!

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:36.540
Sama?!

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:39.220
U-Umm...

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:45.640
A participant from General Studies will have it harder than us, so you've got to support her.

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:47.370
Wh-What?

00:02:49.050 --> 00:02:50.950
We're deeply sorry.

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:53.690
I'm really sorry about that.

00:02:56.830 --> 00:02:58.020
Are you all right?

00:02:58.020 --> 00:03:00.760
I-I-I-I'm fine.

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:02.280
Oh, that's good.

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:03.770
No it isn't!

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:08.500
We want to hear her perform <i>because</i> she's from General Studies!

00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:13.830
She's been chosen over us, who are in the Music Department!

00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:17.580
'Tis a shame that you put her on the spot to play.

00:03:18.270 --> 00:03:20.130
Who the heck are you?

00:03:21.710 --> 00:03:25.400
Nice to meet you! I'm Amo, a second-year, from the Journalism Club.

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:26.900
Going with what we're discussing,

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:29.770
how would you feel about moving the day and place for her to play?

00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:36.400
The Journalism Club would also like to see what skills she has, before the competition.

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:37.760
Fine.

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:39.990
How about in a week?

00:03:39.990 --> 00:03:40.580
Sure.

00:03:40.580 --> 00:03:42.660
You can't decide that for me!

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:45.280
Wouldn't you like to put them in their place for once?

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:46.290
Still...

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:50.700
Well then, we're looking forward to it, Ms. General Studies.

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:55.430
Please excuse us, Yunoki-sama.

00:03:58.090 --> 00:04:01.510
Man, the Guard is always so scary.

00:04:01.510 --> 00:04:02.850
Guard?!

00:04:02.850 --> 00:04:05.200
Yup, the Yunoki Guard.

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:06.780
Yunoki-sempai's?

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:09.090
It's nothing to get all excited about.

00:04:09.650 --> 00:04:13.980
Umm, I am Fuyuumi, a first year.

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:15.970
I'm sorry. This is all because of me...

00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:19.820
No, it's not your fault.

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:23.870
That being said, man, have I painted myself into a corner.

00:04:23.870 --> 00:04:25.730
Damn that fairy!

00:04:25.730 --> 00:04:27.530
Something the matter, Hino-chan?

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:29.470
No, it's nothing.

00:04:29.470 --> 00:04:31.080
Hey, Hino-san!

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:35.060
The Journalism Club has lots they want to ask you!

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:36.750
U-Umm, actually...

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:39.710
S-Sorry! I just remembered something I have to do!

00:04:39.930 --> 00:04:42.010
H-Hold on!

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:43.470
Geez.

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:46.430
I need to have a word with that fairy.

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:49.160
Oh, but the practice room...

00:04:49.160 --> 00:04:50.570
You're interfering with my practice.

00:04:51.220 --> 00:04:53.520
He's probably still in there.

00:04:53.770 --> 00:04:55.230
Then again,

00:04:55.230 --> 00:04:59.820
peeking in from outside is rather pathetic, isn't it?

00:05:04.820 --> 00:05:06.630
Ow...

00:05:06.630 --> 00:05:08.320
What was that?

00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:14.420
Wh-What a pretty boy!

00:05:16.120 --> 00:05:20.670
A blue tie? He must be a first-year in the Music Department.

00:05:20.670 --> 00:05:22.130
Wait, forget that.

00:05:22.810 --> 00:05:24.420
Hey, you there.

00:05:26.850 --> 00:05:29.600
Why are you sleeping here?

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:31.630
I'm not really sure...

00:05:31.630 --> 00:05:32.850
Huh?

00:05:32.850 --> 00:05:36.470
Anyway, you'll catch cold if you sleep here.

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:41.020
Right. Thank you very much.

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:43.150
Is he gonna be OK?

00:05:48.930 --> 00:05:50.860
Is he?

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:17.300
What are you doing out there?

00:07:18.020 --> 00:07:19.820
What song were you playing?

00:07:19.820 --> 00:07:20.380
Huh?

00:07:20.380 --> 00:07:25.660
It's so beautiful. And you're so talented. You surprised me!

00:07:26.080 --> 00:07:29.780
Could you not fawn all over me, please?

00:07:29.780 --> 00:07:31.300
You needn't flatter me.

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:32.940
That's not it.

00:07:33.930 --> 00:07:36.610
The high notes felt so transparent,

00:07:36.610 --> 00:07:39.160
like they were resonating inside my heart...

00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:44.940
I had no idea that the violin could make such beautiful sounds.

00:07:47.790 --> 00:07:51.990
Oh no. Why am I talking like this?

00:07:52.430 --> 00:07:54.860
Sorry, I'm keeping you from practicing, aren't I?

00:07:54.860 --> 00:07:55.900
Bye.

00:08:04.470 --> 00:08:07.300
I can't find that fairy anywhere.

00:08:07.300 --> 00:08:11.480
But, really, that was such lovely music.

00:08:11.480 --> 00:08:15.130
It must be fun to be able to play like that.

00:08:15.570 --> 00:08:19.360
I'll never be able to play like that.

00:08:19.980 --> 00:08:21.580
I mean, before...

00:08:24.050 --> 00:08:25.010
But...

00:08:38.450 --> 00:08:40.990
I played an actual note! Wow!

00:08:42.540 --> 00:08:45.920
Yes, that song he was playing...

00:09:12.130 --> 00:09:14.330
What is it, Hihara?

00:09:14.330 --> 00:09:16.320
Nah, it's nothing.

00:09:29.230 --> 00:09:30.620
What's up?

00:09:31.130 --> 00:09:34.830
I thought I heard something just now.

00:09:56.440 --> 00:09:57.780
I managed to play it.

00:09:57.780 --> 00:09:59.110
Bravo!

00:09:59.580 --> 00:10:01.140
That was lovely!

00:10:01.140 --> 00:10:03.320
Schubert's "Ave Maria," right?

00:10:03.320 --> 00:10:04.910
Ave Maria?

00:10:04.910 --> 00:10:06.570
You didn't know?

00:10:06.570 --> 00:10:11.770
Nope. I just heard someone playing it before and thought it to be very pretty...

00:10:11.770 --> 00:10:16.740
I see. You were feeling in harmony with it, so it came out well.

00:10:16.740 --> 00:10:20.090
But only strange noises came out when I first tried to play it.

00:10:20.090 --> 00:10:22.710
See, even though anyone can play it,

00:10:22.710 --> 00:10:27.220
the magical violin is still basically a set of training wheels for music.

00:10:27.220 --> 00:10:30.610
There's a difference between making noise versus making music.

00:10:32.280 --> 00:10:36.430
Sure, from the standpoint of technique, the violin will support you.

00:10:36.430 --> 00:10:40.700
But it's your feelings that make it really sing.

00:10:41.700 --> 00:10:43.490
In other words, your heart!

00:10:43.940 --> 00:10:46.090
My heart?

00:10:46.090 --> 00:10:49.420
Try your best to duplicate how you felt just now in the competition.

00:10:49.420 --> 00:10:53.460
Hold on a second. There's no way I'm gonna be in the competition.

00:10:53.460 --> 00:10:55.210
Huh? Why not?

00:10:55.480 --> 00:10:57.840
Isn't this unfair to the others?

00:10:57.840 --> 00:11:03.370
I'm not telling you to win! I just want you to enter it.

00:11:03.370 --> 00:11:04.220
Still...

00:11:04.790 --> 00:11:10.070
The man who established this school once saved my life.

00:11:11.400 --> 00:11:14.510
He was a good man who loved music with all his heart.

00:11:15.430 --> 00:11:22.170
So I promised him that I'd grant his school the blessing of music.

00:11:22.170 --> 00:11:25.170
I want to make his dream come true,

00:11:25.170 --> 00:11:27.330
that anyone can come here and study music.

00:11:27.990 --> 00:11:32.250
So, please... Can you help me out?

00:11:36.470 --> 00:11:39.270
There, there, don't cry.

00:11:39.270 --> 00:11:44.300
If it's just participating, then I'll gladly help you.

00:11:45.270 --> 00:11:46.800
You promise?

00:11:46.800 --> 00:11:48.000
Yeah.

00:11:48.650 --> 00:11:50.190
I'm gonna hold you to that!

00:11:51.150 --> 00:11:55.530
All right! You promised me you'd enter the competition!

00:11:55.530 --> 00:11:57.200
What? Hold on...

00:11:57.200 --> 00:12:00.830
Now, practice hard with these!

00:12:08.930 --> 00:12:11.160
My First Violin

00:12:09.240 --> 00:12:11.170
What should I do with these?

00:12:14.380 --> 00:12:16.460
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:12:19.600 --> 00:12:21.990
Was that you playing Ave Maria before?

00:12:21.990 --> 00:12:23.610
Uh, umm...

00:12:23.610 --> 00:12:28.570
You've got a long ways to go if you're going to be in the competition.

00:12:33.440 --> 00:12:36.970
Technically speaking, that is.

00:12:37.890 --> 00:12:39.350
However...

00:12:51.840 --> 00:12:55.000
Umm, all participants in the music competition,

00:12:54.600 --> 00:13:00.590
Conference Room

00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:58.330
please assemble in the Music Department's conference room.

00:12:59.000 --> 00:13:00.590
I'm feeling down...

00:13:01.140 --> 00:13:03.350
Oh, Ms. General Studies.

00:13:03.350 --> 00:13:04.400
Geh!

00:13:04.400 --> 00:13:07.830
Just because Yunoki-sama showed you some graciousness earlier...

00:13:07.830 --> 00:13:09.810
...don't let it go to your head.

00:13:09.810 --> 00:13:14.600
Of course I wouldn't. I don't even really know him...

00:13:14.600 --> 00:13:16.810
You don't know him?!

00:13:17.880 --> 00:13:20.060
Azuma Yunoki-sama...

00:13:20.060 --> 00:13:23.010
He comes from a family of master flower arrangers.

00:13:23.010 --> 00:13:25.550
His grades are always at the top of his class.

00:13:25.550 --> 00:13:28.840
He's kind to all souls. A truly wonderful human being.

00:13:28.840 --> 00:13:34.430
And yet someone you like you will be in the same competition as him!

00:13:34.430 --> 00:13:36.370
What's going on here?

00:13:36.370 --> 00:13:38.390
Oh, Hino-chan!

00:13:38.950 --> 00:13:40.830
Y-Yunoki-sama?

00:13:40.830 --> 00:13:43.290
N-Nothing at all!

00:13:43.290 --> 00:13:44.920
Do excuse us!

00:13:44.920 --> 00:13:46.000
Huh?

00:13:46.720 --> 00:13:48.720
Ah, I'm saved.

00:14:00.630 --> 00:14:02.880
Ah, Hino-sempai...

00:14:02.880 --> 00:14:05.820
OK, that's everyone, huh?

00:14:06.600 --> 00:14:10.820
The Principal said I should at least meet each of you.

00:14:10.820 --> 00:14:14.040
So, let's start the self-introductions from that end.

00:14:14.040 --> 00:14:15.730
Ah, uh...

00:14:15.730 --> 00:14:21.650
I'm Shoko Fuyuumi, from class 1-B. I play the clarinet.

00:14:21.650 --> 00:14:27.800
1-A, Keiichi Shimizu. I play the cello.

00:14:28.070 --> 00:14:31.510
Oh, he's the one who was sleeping in the schoolyard yesterday.

00:14:31.510 --> 00:14:35.880
3-B, Kazuki Hihara. I play the trumpet.

00:14:35.880 --> 00:14:36.850
Nice to meet you!

00:14:36.850 --> 00:14:41.810
Same class, 3-B. I'm Azuma Yunoki. I play the flute.

00:14:42.740 --> 00:14:47.020
2-A, Len Tsukimori. I play the violin.

00:14:48.920 --> 00:14:49.800
Hey.

00:14:51.050 --> 00:14:56.190
Ah, 2-2, Kahoko Hino. The violin.

00:14:56.520 --> 00:14:59.550
All right, that's all six of you.

00:14:59.550 --> 00:15:04.420
Well, the competition will be divided up into four selections.

00:15:05.240 --> 00:15:07.620
You'll be ranked on each selection,

00:15:07.620 --> 00:15:11.610
and we'll use those points to choose the finalists.

00:15:11.610 --> 00:15:15.570
You mean we have to play four different songs?

00:15:15.570 --> 00:15:18.780
Each selection comes with a theme.

00:15:18.780 --> 00:15:23.030
You are free to choose any piece you want, but it must be based on this theme.

00:15:23.030 --> 00:15:26.860
In other words, your interpretation of the piece is also important.

00:15:27.120 --> 00:15:32.730
So, before the ranking, you'll need to strengthen your musical comprehension.

00:15:32.730 --> 00:15:37.140
And more than anything, don't forget to enjoy yourself.

00:15:38.190 --> 00:15:40.280
E-Enjoy myself?

00:15:40.280 --> 00:15:43.040
Like I'll have time to do that!

00:15:48.810 --> 00:15:51.130
You're Hino, right?

00:15:51.130 --> 00:15:52.390
Tsuchiura-kun...

00:15:52.390 --> 00:15:55.760
So you're the General Studies student that's gonna be entering.

00:15:55.760 --> 00:16:00.760
U-Umm, actually... Oh, I didn't know you were on the soccer team!

00:16:02.000 --> 00:16:04.690
Don't try to change the subject.

00:16:04.690 --> 00:16:08.640
But you must be pretty good to make it in from the General Studies program...

00:16:08.640 --> 00:16:09.950
What's wrong?

00:16:09.950 --> 00:16:12.750
Fight, fight, fight, fight!

00:16:12.750 --> 00:16:16.830
What? You're an amateur? Then why?

00:16:16.830 --> 00:16:18.450
U-Umm...

00:16:18.660 --> 00:16:20.210
I saw a fairy.

00:16:20.210 --> 00:16:21.790
The bells rang...

00:16:20.270 --> 00:16:21.790
The Winner

00:16:21.790 --> 00:16:23.950
I was given a magical violin!

00:16:24.720 --> 00:16:27.310
I can't say all that!

00:16:27.310 --> 00:16:28.430
Hino?

00:16:29.330 --> 00:16:36.280
It's my first ever competition, so I'm not sure how to go about it...

00:16:37.950 --> 00:16:41.810
Gavotte, huh? Are you studying that piece?

00:16:41.810 --> 00:16:43.230
No, not yet.

00:16:43.230 --> 00:16:47.850
Then why don't you start by practicing it?

00:16:47.850 --> 00:16:48.950
But...

00:16:49.950 --> 00:16:52.630
Don't be so hard on yourself.

00:16:52.630 --> 00:16:53.780
Huh?

00:16:53.780 --> 00:16:57.780
There must be a good reason why you were chosen.

00:16:57.780 --> 00:17:00.990
If you ever need to talk to someone, let me know.

00:17:01.460 --> 00:17:03.010
Tsuchiura-kun...

00:17:03.510 --> 00:17:04.960
Thank you.

00:17:12.590 --> 00:17:15.380
Oh, so that's Gavotte.

00:17:17.130 --> 00:17:20.220
It's all Greek to me when I look at the score, though.

00:17:20.920 --> 00:17:22.690
Well, I guess I'll give it a shot.

00:17:24.970 --> 00:17:30.860
When I picture the melody, my left and right arms begin moving on their own.

00:17:41.310 --> 00:17:43.860
It's like someone else's arms are playing.

00:17:44.370 --> 00:17:46.740
Though I guess it does play a song, somehow.

00:17:48.220 --> 00:17:50.310
I need to practice more.

00:18:01.220 --> 00:18:02.670
A shoulder pad?

00:18:09.480 --> 00:18:11.510
What? Muscle pain?

00:18:11.510 --> 00:18:12.810
Does your chin hurt?

00:18:24.490 --> 00:18:29.450
Why, I wonder? I was able to play Ave Maria better than this...

00:18:44.140 --> 00:18:46.970
Oh, Hino-chan. What's up?

00:18:47.610 --> 00:18:50.180
Umm, I... I came to practice.

00:18:50.180 --> 00:18:52.730
Oh, right. You have to play tomorrow.

00:18:52.730 --> 00:18:54.370
How are you feeling?

00:18:54.370 --> 00:18:55.450
Not so good.

00:18:55.870 --> 00:18:58.150
Just play like you always do and you'll be fine.

00:18:58.680 --> 00:19:00.460
You say that, but...

00:19:00.460 --> 00:19:01.700
What are you gonna play?

00:19:01.700 --> 00:19:04.370
Umm... Gavotte.

00:19:04.370 --> 00:19:06.740
Gavotte! I've played that before.

00:19:06.740 --> 00:19:09.640
Huh? You can play it on the trumpet too?

00:19:09.640 --> 00:19:11.650
Of course you can!

00:19:11.650 --> 00:19:15.090
Kazuki Hihara shall entertain you with his rendition!

00:19:35.490 --> 00:19:37.180
What's wrong, Hino-chan?!

00:19:37.990 --> 00:19:43.390
No, it's just... You play such an enjoyable rendition of it,

00:19:43.390 --> 00:19:45.170
and mine is completely lousy...

00:19:45.720 --> 00:19:49.370
Don't give me that troubled look, Hino-chan.

00:19:49.950 --> 00:19:53.370
Come on, it's supposed to be a fun song!

00:19:55.000 --> 00:19:57.090
You need to enjoy yourself more!

00:19:58.490 --> 00:20:01.350
Enjoy... myself?

00:20:01.350 --> 00:20:04.930
Oh, but, I'm getting ahead of myself.

00:20:04.930 --> 00:20:07.010
People always tell me not to do that.

00:20:10.520 --> 00:20:13.490
Hey! Don't laugh at me, Hino-chan!

00:20:15.130 --> 00:20:18.120
Thank you so much, Hihara-sempai.

00:20:32.830 --> 00:20:34.450
Kaho-chan...

00:20:34.450 --> 00:20:38.780
This is great... It's like a duel.

00:20:38.780 --> 00:20:42.760
Well, will you play for us, as promised?

00:20:46.290 --> 00:20:47.990
I'm leaving it to you.

00:20:49.500 --> 00:20:51.400
Hihara-sempai's performance...

00:20:51.920 --> 00:20:56.470
He looked like he was enjoying himself so much while playing.

00:20:57.730 --> 00:21:01.740
Just listening to it was such a pleasurable pick-me-up.

00:21:01.740 --> 00:21:05.060
The music leaps up and down during this piece.

00:21:05.060 --> 00:21:06.760
It's so cute.

00:21:11.690 --> 00:21:15.330
Gavotte? Such an easy piece.

00:21:16.310 --> 00:21:18.530
Don't give me that troubled look.

00:21:18.530 --> 00:21:20.930
You need to enjoy yourself more!

00:21:22.840 --> 00:21:25.100
Exactly. It'd be a waste not to.

00:21:29.330 --> 00:21:31.110
Hey, what's going on?

00:21:31.520 --> 00:21:33.150
An impromptu performance?

00:21:33.150 --> 00:21:34.060
Hey, let's watch her.

00:21:40.240 --> 00:21:41.690
When did they all...

00:21:44.580 --> 00:21:45.800
Oh, dear.

00:21:45.800 --> 00:21:49.200
Could you not screw up in such a simple section?

00:21:49.720 --> 00:21:50.920
Kaho...

00:21:52.500 --> 00:21:55.710
Come on, let's hear the rest.

00:21:56.760 --> 00:22:00.670
No... My hands are shaking...

00:22:01.280 --> 00:22:05.310
This is bad... I can't play!

00:23:36.720 --> 00:23:40.350
Lili's One Point Classic!

00:23:36.870 --> 00:23:40.060
Lili's One Point Classic

00:23:40.350 --> 00:23:44.530
Strumming the bow along the strings isn't the only way to play a violin.

00:23:44.530 --> 00:23:47.730
If you pluck a string with a finger on your right hand, it's called a pizzicato.

00:23:47.730 --> 00:23:51.570
And if you hit the strings with part of your bow, it's called a col legno.

00:23:51.570 --> 00:23:56.420
By the way, "corda", like in the title, is this string.

00:23:57.480 --> 00:23:59.220
OK, now time for a quiz.

00:23:59.220 --> 00:24:03.100
What is the string on the bow made out of?

00:24:03.100 --> 00:24:05.440
The answer is at the end of this program!

00:24:05.440 --> 00:24:10.590
Next Episode

00:24:06.940 --> 00:24:10.590
Why do Tsukimori-kun and Tsuchiura-kun not get along?

00:24:10.590 --> 00:24:13.260
Hino, don't say that to anyone!

00:24:13.260 --> 00:24:16.680
Tsuchiura-kun! Don't yell at me during the next episode preview!

00:24:16.680 --> 00:24:19.130
Next episode: The Anonymous Chopin.

